# Unit19
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit19核心词汇

assembly/əˈsembli/集会；装配/The assembly of the machine took two hours.
assertion/əˈsɜːrʃn/断言/His assertion was supported by evidence.
asset/ˈæset/资产/Good employees are a valuable asset to the company.
assimilate/əˈsɪmɪleɪt/同化/Immigrants often assimilate into the local culture.
assumption/əˈsʌmpʃn/假设/Your assumption is not supported by the facts.
asylum/əˈsaɪləm/庇护/He applied for political asylum.
atmosphere/ˈætməsfɪr/气氛；大气层/The atmosphere in the room was tense.
attorney/əˈtɜːrni/律师/She hired an attorney to handle the case.
attribute/əˈtrɪbjuːt/属性/Kindness is her best attribute.
authentic/ɔːˈθentɪk/真实的/This is an authentic Italian restaurant.
authorize/ˈɔːθəraɪz/授权/Only the manager can authorize such a decision.
autonomous/ɔːˈtɑːnəməs/自治的/The region became an autonomous state.
backdrop/ˈbækdrɑːp/背景/The mountains provided a beautiful backdrop.
bail/beɪl/保释/He was released on bail.
bankrupt/ˈbæŋkrʌpt/破产的/The company went bankrupt last year.
barely/ˈberli/仅仅；几乎不/He barely passed the exam.
barrier/ˈbæriər/障碍/There are many barriers to communication.
benchmark/ˈbentʃmɑːrk/基准/The test serves as a benchmark for student performance.
benefactor/ˈbenɪfæktər/捐助者/A wealthy benefactor donated the money.
bizarre/bɪˈzɑːr/奇怪的/He told a bizarre story about his trip.
blaze/bleɪz/火焰/The blaze destroyed the entire building.
bless/bles/祝福/She blessed her children before they left.
blunt/blʌnt/钝的；直率的/He is known for his blunt honesty.
boast/boʊst/夸耀/He boasted about his achievements.
bold/boʊld/大胆的/It was a bold decision to change careers.
bond/bɑːnd/纽带/The bond between them is very strong.
boom/buːm/繁荣/The city experienced an economic boom.
boost/buːst/促进/The tax cut will boost consumer spending.
bound/baʊnd/一定的/He is bound to succeed.
breakthrough/ˈbreɪkθruː/突破/Scientists made a major breakthrough in cancer research.
breed/briːd/品种/This breed of dog is very loyal.
brief/briːf/简短的/He gave a brief summary of the meeting.
brilliant/ˈbrɪliənt/杰出的/She is a brilliant scientist.
broaden/ˈbrɔːdn/拓宽/Travel can broaden your horizons.
brutal/ˈbruːtl/残忍的/The winter was brutal this year.
burden/ˈbɜːrdn/负担/Taxes are a heavy burden on small businesses.
bureau/ˈbjʊroʊ/局/She works at the Bureau of Labor Statistics.
burst/bɜːrst/爆发/The audience burst into applause.
cabinet/ˈkæbɪnɪt/内阁/The president appointed a new cabinet member.
calculate/ˈkælkjuleɪt/计算/Can you calculate the total cost?
campaign/kæmˈpeɪn/运动/The marketing campaign was very successful.
candidate/ˈkændɪdət/候选人/There are five candidates for the position.
capable/ˈkeɪpəbl/有能力的/She is capable of handling any challenge.
capacity/kəˈpæsəti/容量/The stadium has a capacity of 50,000 people.
capture/ˈkæptʃər/捕获/The photographer captured a beautiful moment.
casualty/ˈkæʒuəlti/伤亡/There were no casualties in the accident.
category/ˈkætəɡɔːri/类别/These books fall into different categories.
cease/siːs/停止/The factory ceased operations last year.
census/ˈsensəs/人口普查/The census revealed a population increase.
ceremony/ˈserəmoʊni/典礼/The opening ceremony was very impressive.
